  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/circular.rs`: before each ring after the first, the tool climbs straight up to clearance at the end of the last ring. Then the ring's ladder enters from clearance, as the first ring does. This applies to the flat mode and to the vault.\n- The unit tests of `circular.rs` move to `circular_tests.rs` with no change. This keeps `circular.rs` at 361 lines (it was 411 before this PR).\n- Two goldens gain the one new climb move.\n- New pins in `crates/motion/tests/circular_ring_links.rs` and `crates/app/tests/circular_ring_links.rs`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2898-circular-ring-links.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach ring runs its own level ladder (ring-major order). The first descent of a ladder expects the tool at clearance. After the first ring, the tool stood on that ring's floor. The descent then made one diagonal rapid from the floor up to clearance over the next ring's start. That rapid crossed the core that the next ring had still to cut. Verification convicted it and held the post. A 5 mm hole with a Ø6 tool has only one ring, so the catalog case did not show the fault. The vault had the same diagonal rapid.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `the_link_between_circular_rings_clears_the_stock` (motion): plunge, helix and ramp entry; planar and default links; flat and vault. No lateral rapid under the stock top. The verifier convicts no rapid.\n- `the_issue_case_climbs_to_clearance_between_its_rings` (motion): the issue's four rings (R 7, 5, 3, 1). Each traverse onto R 5, 3 and 1 is at clearance.\n- `a_spliced_diagonal_link_between_rings_is_still_convicted` (motion): the real path is clean. A diagonal link of the old shape, spliced in, gets `RapidInStock`. This is the \"post stays blocked for a deliberately unsafe link\" part of Done.\n- `a_multi_ring_circular_links_its_rings_over_the_stock_and_posts` (app): the issue's job through generate, verify and post. No warning, and the program posts, for the plunge and the ramp entry.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged code the app pin reports `RapidInStock { at: 69 }` and `RapidInStock { at: 119 }`, the moves that the issue names. The motion pin reports rapids under the stock top at moves 69, 119 and 169.\n\nMutation: the fix with the climb disabled makes all three motion pins red (the flat case and the vault case at moves 20 and 40). The fix restored makes them green.\n\nGate:\n\nVerification head: `050d1a7051475c6634e7493b6c8aa7077a959eeb`.\nInvocation base: `upstream/main` at `1d5de9aeb846b83ee69a6cbbfd6f2ee8cdd3230e`.\nThe effective diff merge base was `0b8f4879dd88afe5f658a18c5dde035a88be41e3`.\nThese runs tested the unchanged final head directly.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green. All 240 steps passed in 45.3 minutes.\n- Every reached motion heavy target ran. Its 37 steps had 59 ordinary test passes and two accepted expected-failure controls for #1950.\n- Every reached app heavy target ran. Its 202 steps had 44 ordinary test passes and two accepted expected-failure controls for #1950 and #2849.\n- One shared release build completes the 240 heavy steps. No unexpected failure occurred.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. All 705 steps passed in 42.1 minutes.\n- Motion `circular_ring_links`: all four tests passed, including `a_multi_ring_helix_keeps_both_the_clearance_lift_and_descent_tracking`.\n- App `circular_ring_links`: its generation, verification, and posting test passed.\n- `default_machine_missing`: all nine tests passed, including `a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post_per_operation`.\n- `cargo clippy -j 16 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green in 33 seconds.\n- Heavy used a job budget of 24. Quick used eight jobs and `CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off` while heavy ran concurrently.\n- Clippy ran with quick after heavy finished. No tracked file changed during verification.\n- Another session advanced the local main reference after both gate plans started. The invocation base above applies to both runs.\n- The latest finding required verification evidence. No source edit, new pin, or new mutation check was needed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nTwo goldens. Each gains one line, `Rapid <x> <y> <clearance>`, at the first ring's end, with the same X and Y. The header move count goes up by one. No other line changes.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/circular_ring_arcs.cl`: 401 to 402 moves.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/circular_ramp_stay_down.cl`: 133 to 134 moves.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The helix entry with several rings is still refused. Each ring's helix touches the last ring's helix at the start of the ring, in the same depth band. The crossing law convicts that touch. The program is refused, not unsafe. Follow-up: #3109.\n- I tried the pocket's z-major order for the flat mode on this branch. It removed the helix crossings, but the inner rings then started with an axial plunge that was not named, also under a ramp entry. Four ramp-entry tests went red. I dropped it (see the decision record).\n- Pixel snapshots were not run.\n- This verification used the configured sccache wrapper at `/home/mikekinney/.local/bin/sccache`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2842 changes `crates/motion/src/machining2d/circular.rs` too, in the level ladder calls (`cut_levels_under`, `levels_from`). This PR changes the lines before `run_level_walks` and moves the test module. Touches the same file, different lines; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Circular with several rings no longer links its rings with a rapid through the stock; each ring after the first climbs to clearance first, so verification passes and the program posts.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2898\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
